## Why Asked
Tests fundamental understanding of common web vulnerabilities and their attack vectors.
## Key Concepts
XSS executes client-side scripts, CSRF exploits user authentication, both target different security layers.
## Code Example
```
// XSS prevention
const sanitized = escapeHtml(userInput);

// CSRF prevention
app.use(csrf({ cookie: true }));
```
## Follow-up Questions
How would you prevent each attack type? What are stored vs reflected XSS?
